/>

<!-- 01 ANSWER-FIRST -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · The short answer</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Bosch won't drain? E24 is the path, E25 is the pump.</h2>

    <p><strong>Standing water in a Bosch dishwasher shows as E24 or E25. E24 means the drain path is blocked — the filter first, then the drain hose, air gap, or disposal knockout plug. E25 points at the drain pump itself: a loose pump cover or a jammed impeller. The filter, hose, disposal, air gap, and even unclipping the pump cover to check the impeller are homeowner-checkable — Bosch actually walks owners through it — and replacing the pump is where our techs take over. Start by twisting out and rinsing the filter, Bosch's number-one cause. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</strong></p>

    <p>One thing to get right up front: <strong>E24 and E25 are drain codes, but E15 is not.</strong> E15 is a leak code — water in the base pan trips the safety float — with a different cause and fix. If you're seeing E15, use our <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/bosch-e15-error/">Bosch E15 error</a> page; if the tub is holding water with E24 or E25, keep reading.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 E24 vs E25 -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · E24 vs E25 vs E15</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three codes people mix up.</h2>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>E24 — drain path blocked</h3>
      <p>The water isn't being pumped out. Most often the filter is clogged; then the drain hose (kink or clog), the air gap, or a disposal knockout plug left in. This is the broad "won't drain" code and the one the filter clean usually fixes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>E25 — drain pump blocked</h3>
      <p>Points at the pump: the white pump cover is loose or not seated, or the impeller is jammed by a foreign object (glass, a fruit sticker, a bone chip). Bosch's fix is to unclip the cover, clear debris, and confirm the impeller turns freely.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>E15 — leak, NOT drain</h3>
      <p>Water in the base pan trips the AquaStop float and the unit shuts off its water. Different problem, different page: <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/bosch-e15-error/">Bosch E15 error</a>. Don't chase a drain clog when the code is E15.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 SAFE CHECKS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · What you can safely check</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Six safe steps before you call.</h2>

    <ol class="diag-list">
      <li><strong>Scoop the standing water</strong> with a cup and sponge so you can reach the filter.</li>
      <li><strong>Clean the filter.</strong> Twist out the cylindrical filter (Bosch's #1 step), rinse it, and clear the sump — watch for broken glass.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the pump cover and impeller (E25).</strong> Unclip the white pump cover under the filter, clear any debris, and, wearing a glove, confirm the impeller turns freely.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the drain hose and high loop.</strong> Straighten any kink and confirm the hose loops up high before dropping to the drain.</li>
      <li><strong>Run the garbage disposal</strong> with water, and if it's a new disposal, confirm the knockout plug was removed.</li>
      <li><strong>Clear the air gap.</strong> Pop the chrome cap and clean it out. Use only dishwasher detergent, never dish soap.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Where to stop:</strong> filter, pump cover and impeller check, hose, disposal, and air gap are all owner-safe per Bosch. Do not replace the drain pump, cut into wiring, or do any electrical work. If the impeller won't turn freely after clearing debris, or E24/E25 returns with everything clear, the pump needs replacing — our job.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 WHEN TO CALL -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">04 · When to call us</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Impeller jammed or won't spin? Time for the pump.</h2>

    <p>Once the filter, hose, disposal, and air gap are verified clear, the pump cover is seated, and the impeller either won't turn or E24/E25 keeps returning, the drain pump has failed and needs replacement — a job that requires removing the pump and disconnecting power. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair carry the common Bosch drain pumps, so a confirmed failure is usually a one-visit fix. We check the upstream path and the impeller first so we never swap a good pump that was fighting a clog, then quote before any work. <strong>$89 residential diagnostic, waived with the repair.</strong> Same-day across <a href="/los-angeles/dishwasher-repair/">Los Angeles</a>, Orange, and Ventura in most cases.</p>

    <p>Related: the <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/bosch-e15-error/">Bosch E15 error</a> page (the leak code), the general <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/not-draining/">dishwasher not draining</a> page, the <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/error-codes/">dishwasher error codes</a> guide, and brand coverage on <a href="/brands/bosch-dishwasher-repair/">Bosch dishwasher repair</a>. Full coverage on the <a href="/services/dishwasher-repair/">dishwasher repair</a> hub. <a href="/book/">Book online</a> or call {phone}.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 FAQ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">05 · FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Bosch dishwasher not draining: common questions.</h2>
